│  ❯ Q1  Should the endpoint send one JSON response with a kind field, and send
│        redirects as a 200 response body that page.tsx acts on?
│
│    A ○ A 200 response like {kind: "redirect", location, permanent}. page.tsx
│        calls permanentRedirect() (308) or redirect(). The redirect is cached per
│        URL like any other result.  Recommended
│    B ○ Django answers with a real 301, and the Next.js fetch reads the Location
│        header: simpler for legacy callers, as the RFC has it.
│        The CmsPageModal keeps reading Location, and nothing in the legacy code
│        changes.
│    C ○ Write your own answer
│    Note: Add a note
│
│    Recommended: A. The redirect stays inside the cached result, and the legacy
│    CmsPageModal can simply ignore that kind.


